From 5096b57cd1677362b83646d3546d5989fc4cc385 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kernel Sprint <kernel-sprint@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 09:27:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: reduce base slice for lower wake-up latency

sysctl_sched_base_slice controls the EEVDF requested time slice used
to compute each sched_entity deadline (deadline = vruntime + slice /
weight). Under CPU contention, a newly-woken task waits for the
currently running task to reach its deadline before it can be picked
by pick_eevdf(), so this constant directly bounds wake-up latency.

Reduce it from the upstream default of 700us to 300us to lower
wake-up latency for latency-sensitive workloads, at the cost of more
frequent context switches. The EEVDF picking algorithm itself
(__pick_eevdf()) and its fairness/eligibility rules are unchanged --
this only retunes an existing constant.

Measured with benchmark/scheduler_latency.c under 4-way CPU
contention: see results/baseline/ vs results/optimized/ in the
kernel-sprint project for before/after numbers.

Signed-off-by: Kernel Sprint <kernel-sprint@example.invalid>
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index c3a6b66b8..1543111bf 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -73,10 +73,10 @@ unsigned int sysctl_sched_tunable_scaling = SCHED_TUNABLESCALING_LOG;
 /*
  * Minimal preemption granularity for CPU-bound tasks:
  *
- * (default: 0.70 msec * (1 + ilog(ncpus)), units: nanoseconds)
+ * (kernel-sprint: reduced from upstream 0.70 msec to 0.30 msec, units: nanoseconds)
  */
-unsigned int sysctl_sched_base_slice			= 700000ULL;
-static unsigned int normalized_sysctl_sched_base_slice	= 700000ULL;
+unsigned int sysctl_sched_base_slice			= 300000ULL;
+static unsigned int normalized_sysctl_sched_base_slice	= 300000ULL;
 
 /*
  * After fork, child runs first. If set to 0 (default) then
-- 
